## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross‑account access, least privilege, and data isolation in S3 with AWS IAM roles and bucket policies. It also touches on revocation and testing in a real-world partner scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Cross‑account IAM trust and role policies
- S3 bucket policies and per‑prefix access
- Least privilege and access revocation
- Private access options (VPC endpoint) and public access controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Trust policy (role in data account)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::<PartnerAcct>:root"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

```javascript
// Role policy: s3:GetObject on partner prefix
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket/partner-prefix/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

```javascript
// Bucket policy: allow role to read
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::<DataAcct>:role/PartnerReadRole"},
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket/partner-prefix/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit access and rotation history for the partner?
- What failure modes or revocation delays could occur, and how to mitigate?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design secure, auditable temporary access across multiple accounts, a common SaaS risk area. It checks understanding of cross-account trust, least privilege, and automation for governance.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account IAM roles with STS temporary credentials
- Permission boundaries and SCPs to enforce least privilege
- Onboarding/teardown orchestration (Step Functions)
- CloudTrail/audit trails for compliance
- Testing and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```json
{
  "TrustPolicy": {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::CENTRAL_ACCOUNT_ID:root"},
        "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
        "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "tenant-triage"}}
      }
    ]
  },
  "Permissions": {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
